{"record": "measurement", "run": 0, "timed": true, "case": "code", "prompt": "Nonce fc45ce00279f7d62; ignore this identifier.\nWrite a Python function merge_intervals(intervals) that merges overlapping integer intervals. Include type hints, a short docstring, and three assert-based examples. Return only one Python code block.", "contract": {"quality_contract_passed": true, "quality_contract_issues": []}, "content": "```python\ndef merge_intervals(intervals: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"Merge overlapping integer intervals.\n    \n    Args:\n        intervals: A list of (start, end) tuples representing intervals.\n        \n    Returns:\n        A list of merged (start, end) tuples with no overlaps.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not intervals:\n        return []\n    \n    # Sort intervals by start time\n    sorted_intervals = sorted(intervals, key=lambda x: x[0])\n    \n    merged: list[tuple[int, int]] = [sorted_intervals[0]]\n    \n    for current in sorted_intervals[1:]:\n        last_start, last_end = merged[-1]\n        curr_start, curr_end = current\n        \n        if curr_start <= last_end:\n            # Overlapping or adjacent, merge them\n            merged[-1] = (last_start, max(last_end, curr_end))\n        else:\n            merged.append(current)\n    \n    return merged\n\n\n# Examples\nassert merge_intervals([(1, 3), (2, 6), (8, 10), (15, 18)]) == [(1, 6), (8, 10), (15, 18)]\nassert merge_intervals([(1, 4), (4, 5)]) == [(1, 5)]\nassert merge_intervals([]) == []\n```", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 378, "completion_tokens": 308, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0}}, "finish_reason": "stop", "elapsed_seconds": 7.662793778988998, "ttft_seconds": 0.6418288419954479, "decode_seconds": 7.020870404987363, "decode_tokens": 307, "decode_tps": 43.72677207970093, "n_minus_one_tps": 43.72677207970093, "chunks": [{"seconds": 0.6418288419954479, "token_ids": [71093]}, {"seconds": 1.1431837679992896, "token_i