{"record": "measurement", "run": 0, "timed": true, "case": "fable", "prompt": "Nonce d114b1d9d0eadf46; ignore this identifier.\nWrite a self-contained fable of 140 to 170 words about two parrots who disagree about sharing credit. End with a one-sentence moral.", "contract": {"quality_contract_passed": false, "quality_contract_issues": ["fable has 176 words, outside 140..170"]}, "content": "In the vibrant canopy of the Amazon, two parrots, Zephyr and Zola, discovered a rare, glowing fruit. Zephyr, eager for glory, claimed he spotted it first, puffing his chest feathers proudly. Zola, however, insisted she had guided them through the thorny vines to reach the prize. Their argument grew loud, echoing through the trees, as each parrot demanded sole credit for the discovery. They squabbled over who was the true finder, ignoring the fruit’s delicate skin. In their heated debate, they forgot to watch their footing. A sudden gust of wind shook the branch, and the glowing fruit tumbled into the river below, lost forever. Both parrots stared in silence at the empty branch, realizing their greed had cost them the reward. They had been so busy arguing over who deserved the praise that they failed to appreciate the moment together. The fruit was gone, and so was their chance to share its sweetness. They learned that cooperation yields more than competition.\n\nMoral: Sharing credit strengthens bonds, while hoarding glory often leads to mutual loss.", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 293, "completion_tokens": 225, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0}}, "finish_reason": "stop", "elapsed_seconds": 7.649566929991124, "ttft_seconds": 0.1924810029740911, "decode_seconds": 7.457009312027367, "decode_tokens": 224, "decode_tps": 30.03885212248719, "n_minus_one_tps": 30.03885212248719, "chunks": [{"seconds": 0.1924810029740911, "token_ids": [623]}, {"seconds": 0.25807812498533167, "token_ids": [279, 31883, 60847]}, {"seconds": 0.3242216669896152, "token_ids":